            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present disclosure provides a phase-locked loop (30) including a voltage controlled oscillator (32). The voltage controlled oscillator includes an inductor (50) and a capacitor (52) connected in parallel with a negative resistance structure. The negative resistance structure exhibits tunable capacitance such that frequency of an output (38) can be tuned by a control input signal generated in the phase-locked loop. A phase of a signal derived from the output is compared with a reference signal, and a resulting phase error signal is passed to a filter to derive the control input signal. The negative resistance structure includes first and second transistors (60, 62) with cross-coupled conduction paths between transistor terminals and control terminals. The control terminal of at least one transistor is biased by the control input signal such that parasitic capacitance can be tuned to control the output frequency.</p>
            </abstract>
